steps.do:
Check each requirement:
- the card belongs to the verified user;
- the card is ACTIVE or PENDING (k_card);
- no pending transactions (k_pending);
- no pending refunds: ask the customer (info pending_refunds), because no lookup reads refunds. If one is pending, they must wait for it (typically 3-5 business days) or acknowledge in writing that it goes to the checking account;
- card age: for lost, stolen or fraud_suspected, the 14-day minimum does not apply. For other reasons the card must have been active at least 14 days, counted from date_issued to today (r_time).
If any requirement fails, tell the customer what must be resolved (for card age, give the earliest eligible date) and do not close.

Confirm the closure:
- the card is permanently deactivated and cannot be reactivated;
- recurring payments linked to it must be updated with new payment details;
- a new card can be ordered through the standard process.
For fraud_suspected, also recommend changing the online banking password, and advise reviewing recent transactions and disputing any unauthorized charges.
